    "description": "The Telemetry Distribution Gateway receives events from collectors running across many customer sites. It must deliver events to a changing set of regional storage clusters, alerting services, and audit sinks. Teams add or retire sinks, shift a percentage of traffic to a new cluster, and temporarily increase throttling during peak load. These changes must take effect without deploying the gateway or restarting publishers. A Route Administration component stores ordered rules containing tenant, facility, event category, destination, and rollout percentage; the gateway reloads a versioned ruleset atomically and applies it to subsequent messages. Invalid rule versions must be rejected before activation, and each accepted version must be auditable. Publishers know only the single ingress endpoint and never maintain destination lists. The decision must remain centralized so operators can change topology while producers and consumers remain unaware of it.",
    "decision_statement": "Maintain routing rules in reloadable configuration so destinations and traffic allocations can change while the running gateway continues processing messages.",
    "notes": "Primary dynamic-router because destinations and traffic allocations must change via reloadable versioned rules without redeploying the gateway; content-based-router stays as the near miss for the stable-rule reading and control-bus as supporting for the administered rule lifecycle."
  },
